            },
            {
                "entry_id": "7dfb9243-ffbf-3cad-bac4-0fbd68cf2b66",
                "word": "retranchement",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5d7cdcbc-3bf2-4ebb-9123-393890633088",
                        "entry_id": "7dfb9243-ffbf-3cad-bac4-0fbd68cf2b66",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "retranchements"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9a5abadb-1414-36b3-95db-3de05e3a76d3",
                        "entry_id": "7dfb9243-ffbf-3cad-bac4-0fbd68cf2b66",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Suppression d’une partie d’un tout."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "db40c2c0-f1a1-4666-8a4d-1979f4d62e06",
                                "sense_id": "9a5abadb-1414-36b3-95db-3de05e3a76d3",
                                "text": "On ne peut contester que, le budget s'établissant en Conseil des ministres, mes collègues avaient toute latitude pour protester, pour démissionner au besoin, s'ils jugeaient que les retranchements de crédits que je leur imposais compromettaient les grands intérêts dont ils avaient la garde."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "29c5f424-13e9-3e2a-a62b-142cf5432280",
                        "entry_id": "7dfb9243-ffbf-3cad-bac4-0fbd68cf2b66",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Suppression d’une partie d’un tout.",
                            "Punition consistant en la suppression partielle de la ration de vivres ou d’eau pour une durée plus ou moins longue."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "especially"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6833f001-13c9-4a32-85b7-8768ed5667dc",
                                "sense_id": "29c5f424-13e9-3e2a-a62b-142cf5432280",
                                "text": "D'abord les pauvres exilés de l’île La Mère furent condamnés au travail obligatoire . Ils refusèrent en demandant à être jugés ; des menaces et de légers retranchements de ration furent la conséquence de ce premier refus. Puis le vin fut supprimé."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3b9105c4-e623-3691-ba18-d2d739b9eef1",
                        "entry_id": "7dfb9243-ffbf-3cad-bac4-0fbd68cf2b66",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Suppression totale."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d56b5878-d82b-4698-b2b0-e3318073e6bb",
                                "sense_id": "3b9105c4-e623-3691-ba18-d2d739b9eef1",
                                "text": "Le retranchement de sa pension le réduit à la misère."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6b0fd0be-7d8d-4191-8926-f341dfc3effe",
                                "sense_id": "3b9105c4-e623-3691-ba18-d2d739b9eef1",
                                "text": "C’est le retranchement des vaines richesses et des plaisirs trompeurs, qui leur conserve cette paix, cette union et cette liberté."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d0ab3738-8c6b-31cd-81c2-9ee53e36fa55",
                        "entry_id": "7dfb9243-ffbf-3cad-bac4-0fbd68cf2b66",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tout ce qu’on a retranché d’une chambre ou de toute autre pièce, soit pour lui donner une meilleure proportion, soit pour lui procurer quelque commodité."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f99ec911-0248-42a1-b548-1e9841e89d8d",
                                "sense_id": "d0ab3738-8c6b-31cd-81c2-9ee53e36fa55",
                                "text": "Voici ce qui arriva : à huit heures et demie, dans un moment où mademoiselle Bérard parlait à la vieille portière, Anne-Marie fit passer dans la cour Leuwen qui, deux minutes après, fut placé dans un retranchement en bois peint qui occupait la moitié de l’antichambre de madame de Chasteller."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ef88d3b8-ffa5-3d55-abe4-19e164aeff87",
                        "entry_id": "7dfb9243-ffbf-3cad-bac4-0fbd68cf2b66",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tout ouvrage fait pour fortifier un poste ou pour en augmenter la défense."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d4a7b98-e71c-48cc-85f9-84a7f95604cb",
                                "sense_id": "ef88d3b8-ffa5-3d55-abe4-19e164aeff87",
                                "text": "[…] ; aidé par le capitaine, il fit abattre une énorme quantité d’arbres afin de former un solide retranchement hérissé de chevaux de frise. Derrière le retranchement, les lanceros creusèrent un large fossé dont ils rejetèrent la terre du côté du camp, puis derrière ce deuxième retranchement les ballots furent empilés de façon à former une troisième et dernière enceinte."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d3ecc41-356b-4196-9f8c-de70ca277a29",
                                "sense_id": "ef88d3b8-ffa5-3d55-abe4-19e164aeff87",
                                "text": "Aussitôt le colonel Lamoricière et des officiers du génie et de Zouaves, suivis de leurs troupes, sortent rapidement du retranchement avec une sorte d'impétuosité contenue et disciplinée, et se portent au pas de course jusqu'au pied de la brèche."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "785294f3-fd9d-434a-90c9-ade2a4c6d984",
                                "sense_id": "ef88d3b8-ffa5-3d55-abe4-19e164aeff87",
                                "text": "Près de Maidstone, ils tombèrent sur une rangée de onze canons automobiles de construction spéciale, autour desquels des artilleurs affairés surveillaient avec des jumelles une sorte de retranchement qu’on établissait sur la crête de la colline."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "050d181f-8c0b-3cca-a298-3b55cc81c4ec",
                        "entry_id": "7dfb9243-ffbf-3cad-bac4-0fbd68cf2b66",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tout dispositif de défense."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "figuratively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d1d682d-ef17-4f47-be6a-2d913a8b82ca",
                                "sense_id": "050d181f-8c0b-3cca-a298-3b55cc81c4ec",
                                "text": "Elle organisait notre retranchement : barres de fer aux fenêtres et aux portes, tous les verrous tirés, tous les cadenas cadenassés et, pour plus de sûreté, une fois les domestiques enfermés avec nous, chargés de paniers et de vivres, elle faisait pousser les gros meubles devant les ouvertures les plus fragiles."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6d7b49c2-937d-4936-ac84-68c0bbfe51bd",
                        "source_entry_id": "7dfb9243-ffbf-3cad-bac4-0fbd68cf2b66",
                        "target_lang_word": "retrenchment",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "retrenchment",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0f2d3f5-b87b-3d2f-af20-12824fa85206",
                                        "entry_id": "b316c21e-9ef0-3b11-b5e3-2cc7fdd449fa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A curtailment or reduction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b95b3fb-1beb-433f-9a4a-08fb18a92399",
                                                "sense_id": "f0f2d3f5-b87b-3d2f-af20-12824fa85206",
                                                "text": "It agrees that redundant services should not be continued but is not unmindful of the fact that too much retrenchment of rail services now may ultimately prove detrimental to the economy of the country."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4665e66-4e54-4277-bbe6-722e52e804eb",
                                                "sense_id": "f0f2d3f5-b87b-3d2f-af20-12824fa85206",
                                                "text": "Last year it was announced that electrification of L.M.R. main lines was to be speeded up and that it would be essential for the engineers to have the longest possible occupation of the lines involved; this would mean some retrenchment of passenger train services."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d6e185e-2091-4e7c-a2e4-1b61c0d2ef6a",
                                                "sense_id": "f0f2d3f5-b87b-3d2f-af20-12824fa85206",
                                                "text": "And the retrenchment of services such as mental health and drug rehabilitation means that vulnerable people are more likely to find themselves on the street."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9e7b6dc1-bb44-3c34-bf84-fbb949cbbfbf",
                                        "entry_id": "b316c21e-9ef0-3b11-b5e3-2cc7fdd449fa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A curtailment or reduction.",
                                            "An act of reducing expenses; economizing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "specifically",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d9d8a0e-3c73-4606-bf7f-ba525f867f25",
                                                "sense_id": "9e7b6dc1-bb44-3c34-bf84-fbb949cbbfbf",
                                                "text": "Must my anxious management, my prudent retrenchments, dear Margaretta's savings, all go!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0dbb4545-8db8-4e09-8cf6-77a008270361",
                                                "sense_id": "9e7b6dc1-bb44-3c34-bf84-fbb949cbbfbf",
                                                "text": "From this time, the hand which had ever been ready to supply all our wants real or imaginary, opened less promptly at our demands. My father talked occasionally of retrenchment and economy when some of our extravagant bills came in; but we paid little heed to his remarks on this head. Where could we retrench? In what could we economize? The very idea was absurd."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d195f41-ce77-3b99-89f7-622ffef7469d",
                                        "entry_id": "b316c21e-9ef0-3b11-b5e3-2cc7fdd449fa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A curtailment or reduction.",
                                            "An act of terminating the employment of a worker or making an employee redundant, often to reduce expenses; a layoff."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "specifically",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "041d1f67-1a32-3be9-9c3f-1af23e640d1f",
                                        "entry_id": "b316c21e-9ef0-3b11-b5e3-2cc7fdd449fa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Withdrawal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b9717b6-3a71-49e8-b679-635a4485a645",
                                                "sense_id": "041d1f67-1a32-3be9-9c3f-1af23e640d1f",
                                                "text": "Even then—10 long years ago—our disillusionment over past failures, our revulsion against moralistic posturing, our retrenchment from prescribing what was best for other people, our withdrawal symptoms from the exhilarations of overcommitment—all these argued for the perspective of diversity; for lowering our goals."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0caebd69-6c59-486a-b354-fdb052b40186",
                                                "sense_id": "041d1f67-1a32-3be9-9c3f-1af23e640d1f",
                                                "text": "If it is allowed, however, that the theatre of cosmic evolution is endowed with some fixed structure, even a very weak one, then there is a retrenchment from the programme of an evolutionary account of every general law."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e72b5a6-392f-496f-bae6-289b077701c1",
                                                "sense_id": "041d1f67-1a32-3be9-9c3f-1af23e640d1f",
                                                "text": "Given the current retrenchment of liberal internationalism, it is easy to forget that only three decades ago many believed that liberalism had attained a historically definitive victory over all alternatives."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "retrenchment",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "55376f3b-97ff-3cbb-bcd1-953f2785853a",
                                        "entry_id": "b0435b76-9816-3bbc-ab25-9247589c7ffa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A defensive work constructed within a fortification to make it more defensible by allowing defenders to retreat into and fight from it even after the enemy has taken the outer work."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28c10318-1aff-4148-bbe6-1ed23284726b",
                                                "sense_id": "55376f3b-97ff-3cbb-bcd1-953f2785853a",
                                                "text": "The Half-Moon is a Work always raiſed before the Baſtion's Point, being ſo named from the Lowneſs of its Gorges Cavity, &c. and is to ſecure the Two Faces of the Baſtion; but when the Faces have but a weak Defence from the Ravelin, theſe Works are ſoon made uſeleſs or ruined, and give the Beſieged an opportunity of Lodgment, and may ſerve for Batteries and Flanks againſt the oppoſing Baſtions; however they may be retrenched by Traverſes, yet they will not fail to attack entirely in the Face, or where you have your laſt Retrenchment, alſo that called the Counterguard runs the like Hazard."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b43c90c7-6834-45ef-97b4-24af0c0292aa",
                                                "sense_id": "55376f3b-97ff-3cbb-bcd1-953f2785853a",
                                                "text": "[I]f there is one Retrenchment in a Work, it is generally thought ſufficient; but it happens much oftener than there is none at all; ſo that one might be apt to think, a Defence like that we have been explaining is only chimerical, if the Sieges of Vienna and Candy, both by the Turks, were not inſtances of the contrary, where there was hardly an inch of Ground either within or without thoſe two Towns, as far as the Extremities of the Glacis, and even beyond them, but what was retrenched and countermined."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e8e3e05-e47e-4f7b-b723-c35eeea8bdc1",
                                                "sense_id": "55376f3b-97ff-3cbb-bcd1-953f2785853a",
                                                "text": "The gate-way of the north ſide, from whence the garriſon got their water, was near the n. w. angle, and about 80 yards from the river; on the ſide of which, oppoſite to the gate, they threw up a retrenchment, in which they kept a guard to protect the water-carriers."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "retrenchment",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a5e4f19b-e7b6-3560-a6e0-04c2ff38cc47",
                                        "entry_id": "3d91f34e-70e5-3956-a9de-c814730d4b25",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The adoption of a defensive and hostile posture; refusal to compromise, radicalization."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "especially",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "237008dc-e585-4c72-85dc-8749a8365d8e",
                                                "sense_id": "a5e4f19b-e7b6-3560-a6e0-04c2ff38cc47",
                                                "text": "Confronted by their practices again and again, these individuals and organizations in the gay community have made token gestures to appease the demands of people of color, while in the long run these confrontations have resulted in retrenchment of attitudes and stereotypes by gay whites."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac61c06a-236d-43cc-a649-a00228e16a83",
                                                "sense_id": "a5e4f19b-e7b6-3560-a6e0-04c2ff38cc47",
                                                "text": "Retrenchment—on the left and the right—led to exclusivist, mutually recriminating positions on the film that made reasoned debate almost impossible, as opponents drowned each other out with competing narratives of “victimization” and “pariah” status."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e94203fa-136f-4b51-a32b-c422a6b0bd1f",
                                                "sense_id": "a5e4f19b-e7b6-3560-a6e0-04c2ff38cc47",
                                                "text": "But at the Seventeenth CCP Congress in 2008 Zeng Qinghong retired, and beginning the very next year the CCP began a deep political retrenchment, halting most of the political reforms, and reverted to old-style harsh and repressive rule."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "99755ae0-491f-47b0-84a3-512d76a5f5f8",
                                                "sense_id": "a5e4f19b-e7b6-3560-a6e0-04c2ff38cc47",
                                                "text": "While Kim Jong-un has experimented with such reforms, the character of the young leader’s reign has been one of traditionalist retrenchment and the cult of personality."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61f7b3d2-70fc-45e7-ae8c-8c5acc810ea0",
                                                "sense_id": "a5e4f19b-e7b6-3560-a6e0-04c2ff38cc47",
                                                "text": "What was once a conservative retrenchment against civil litigation in the United States has now been globalized in no small part due to the proliferation of class actions as legal transplants."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "62dc6046-1af1-469a-a5c9-93f07498a41f",
                        "source_entry_id": "7dfb9243-ffbf-3cad-bac4-0fbd68cf2b66",
